elinarcurios.beamvoid.desc.storage.0=Stores all 19 particle types, each capped at 9223372036854775807.
elinarcurios.beamvoid.desc.storage.1=Left-click with a Data Stick, then right-click an input/output hatch to link.
elinarcurios.beamvoid.desc.storage.2=Does not create particles: only collects, stores and supplies.
elinarcurios.beamvoid.desc.storage.3=Contents are saved into the dropped item and restored when placed again.
elinarcurios.beamvoid.desc.storage.4=No energy/focus stored: set them on the output hatch.
elinarcurios.beamvoid.desc.input.0=Fits the beam output hatch position of multiblocks (LHC filtered slots included).
elinarcurios.beamvoid.desc.input.1=Once linked, every received beam is stored immediately; accepts all 19 types.
elinarcurios.beamvoid.desc.input.2=Unlinked: behaves like the vanilla filtered beam output hatch (pushes downstream).
elinarcurios.beamvoid.desc.input.3=Data Stick: left-click storage, right-click this hatch; sneak-right-click to unlink.
elinarcurios.beamvoid.desc.input.4=GT beams arrive once per second, so at most one packet per second.
elinarcurios.beamvoid.desc.output.0=Fits the beam input hatch position of multiblocks (LHC / LINAC / Target Chamber).
elinarcurios.beamvoid.desc.output.1=Sends one packet per second: one particle type, energy in eV, rate per second.
elinarcurios.beamvoid.desc.output.2=Focus is fixed at 99. Energy is entered in eV and converted to keV internally.
elinarcurios.beamvoid.desc.output.3=Two switches (OR): emit when the machine is ready, or when redstone powered.
elinarcurios.beamvoid.desc.output.4=Data Stick: left-click storage, right-click this hatch; sneak-right-click to unlink.
elinarcurios.beamvoid.desc.chamber.0=1x1 block: pipe the beam into its front face, particles go into the storage.
elinarcurios.beamvoid.desc.chamber.1=Once linked, every packet is stored immediately; accepts all 19 particle types.
elinarcurios.beamvoid.desc.chamber.2=Unlinked: only displays the last packet, stores nothing.
elinarcurios.beamvoid.desc.chamber.3=Data Stick: left-click storage, right-click this block; sneak-right-click to unlink.
elinarcurios.beamvoid.desc.chamber.4=Reconnects automatically after the storage is moved (by UUID).
